      "text": "To find the value of \\((-1) \\Diamond 6\\) using the operation \\(\\Diamond\\) defined by \\(a \\Diamond b = ab^2 - b + 1\\), we will substitute \\(a = -1\\) and \\(b = 6\\) into the expression.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) into the expression:\n\\[\n(-1) \\Diamond 6 = (-1)(6^2) - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(6^2\\):\n\\[\n6^2 = 36\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(36\\) back into the expression:\n\\[\n(-1)(36) - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nNext, perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n(-1)(36) = -36\n\\]\n\nReplace the multiplication back into the expression:\n\\[\n-36 - 6 + 1\n\\]\n\nThen, perform the subtraction and addition from left to right:\n\\[\n-36 - 6 = -42\n\\]\n\\[\n-42 + 1 = -41\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\((-1) \\Diamond 6\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-41}\n\\]",
